abstract: >
  A source-trust-isolating benchmark and pipeline for epistemic fact verification,
  grounded in the Indian Pramana epistemology. The framework assigns each evidence
  item an Epistemic Confidence score (EC = 1 - (1 - ST)^(EW * IS)) derived from
  source trust, evidence-type weight, and inference strength, and trains heterogeneous
  graph neural networks to reason over this signal. The v3 benchmark isolates source
  trust as the sole label-determining feature by holding evidence text byte-identical
  across trust tiers, demonstrating a sharp inversion: trust-blind models collapse to
  chance (macro-F1 0.381) while trust-aware models win (v2-HGNN 0.924 ± 0.005).
  Mid-tier boundary probes reveal that continuous trust reasoning is required, not
  mere thresholding.
